This package contains the following files:

1. strips.pl - version 1.1 of planner R in SWI-PROLOG. It works for
   STRIPS domains only.
2. bin/pddl2lower - tcl script that converts all upper case letters
   to lower case ones, and replaces "-" by "U" and "_" by "V" in the input
   file. Usage: pddl2lower inputfile outputfile
3. bin/pl2pddl - the almost reverse of pddl2lower. It replaces "U" by "-"
   and "V" by "_". It reads from standard input and writes to the standard
   output.
4. r.execute - tcl script for running the planner. Usage:
   r.execute path prob1 prob2 ... probk
   where "path" is the directory where there is a "domain.pddl" file that
   specifies the action domain in PDDL format, and "prob1",..., "probk" are
   files in the directory "path" that are problem descriptions in PDDL
   format.
5. examples/blocks/ - the blocks world domain at AIPS-2000 competition.
6. examples/log/ - the logistics world domain at AIPS-2000 competition.
7. run-blocks - sample tcl script for solving all the problems in
   examples/blocks
8. t.pl - SWI-Prolog program used by monitor.
9. monitor - tcl script for monitoring the time spent on solving a problem.
   The max time is set to be 10000 seconds. For this program to work, there
   should be no other SWI-Prolog processes running by the user except that
   started by r.execute.
10. block-control.pl - control information for the blocks world.
11. run-blocks-control - tcl script for solving the blocks world problem
    using control information in blocks-control.pl.
12. log-control.pl - control information for the logistics domain.
13. log-control2.pl - another version of control information for the
    logistics domain.
14. logistics - logistics domain specification automatically generated
    from corresponding typed PDDL specifications.
15. r-present.ps - PostScript file of the slides of a talk given at the 
    University of Toronto in June 2000.

The Prolog programs require SWI-Prolog 3.2.9 which can be downloaded
from SWI-Prolog's home page: 
http://www.swi.psy.uva.nl/projects/SWI-Prolog/download.html
